How can you, you be so cruel to say that my life is benefiting from my suffering? And I wrote to her right back and said, you know, I know there's a distinction there, which I actually make, which is chosen suffering, I think, has a lot of benefits and there's a lot of value. Unchosen suffering is a very mixed back. Unchosen suffering. And, you know, we're living in a pandemic. There's plenty of unchosen suffering around. But it's by no means clear unchosen suffering has to benefit of chosen suffering. Now, when I say this, I bump up against people and, you know, some really respected scholars, psychologists, psychiatrists who say, no, very often unchosen suffering the death of a child, a serious illness, something your house burns down, you lose your job,
你怎么能如此残忍地说我的生活从我的苦难中受益？我立刻回信给她说，你知道，我知道那里有一个区别，我实际上也提到了，那就是选择的苦难，我认为有很多好处，有很多价值。未选择的苦难是一个非常混合的包。未选择的苦难。而且，你知道，我们生活在大流行中。周围有很多未选择的苦难。但未选择的苦难绝不一定有选择的苦难的好处。现在，当我这么说时，我与人发生冲突，你知道，一些非常受人尊敬的学者、心理学家、精神病学家说，不，很多时候未选择的苦难，孩子的死亡、严重的疾病、你的房子被烧毁、你失业，

23
