has benefits. They call it post-traumatic growth to distinguish it from post-traumatic stress disorder. But I got to say, I'm a skeptic. I review a literature in my book saying that, although people often think that bad experiences make them stronger, and I'd be crazy to. to deny that in some cases a bad experience could make you stronger. People are complicated. There's no regular rule that bad things are good for you. The good news is we seem to be very resilient. Bad things don't hurt us as much as we often think they will. But bad experiences are actually, for the most part, not good for us. And to say otherwise is wishful thinking. And I also think it's, I think it's something important to get right. Because if you're wrong and you tell
有好处。他们称之为“创伤后成长”，以区别于“创伤后应激障碍”。但我必须说，我是一个怀疑论者。我在书中回顾了文献，说虽然人们经常认为糟糕的经历使他们变得更强大，如果我否认在某些情况下糟糕的经历可以使你变得更强大，那我就疯了。人是复杂的。没有规律说坏事对你有好处。好消息是我们似乎非常有韧性。坏事对我们的伤害并没有我们通常认为的那么大。但糟糕的经历实际上，在很大程度上，对我们没有好处。说反话是痴心妄想。而且我也认为，我认为这是一件需要正确对待的重要事情。因为如果你错了，你告诉

